  "generated_text": "1. **Define the variables:**\n   Let \\( s \\) be the length of a side of the square in inches.\n\n2. **Set up the equation:**\n   The perimeter \\( P \\) of the square is given by \\( P = 4s \\).\n   The area \\( A \\) of the square is given by \\( A = s^2 \\).\n   According to the problem, \\( P = A \\).\n\n3. **Substitute the expressions for \\( P \\) and \\( A \\):**\n   \\[\n   4s = s^2\n   \\]\n\n4. **Solve the equation:**\n   Rearrange the equation to form a quadratic equation:\n   \\[\n   s^2 - 4s = 0\n   \\]\n   Factor out \\( s \\):\n   \\[\n   s(s - 4) = 0\n   \\]\n   This gives us two solutions: \\( s = 0 \\) or \\( s = 4 \\). Since \\( s = 0 \\) is not a valid solution for a square, we have \\( s = 4 \\).\n\n5. **Conclusion:**\n   The length of a side of the square is $\\boxed{4}$ inches.",
